{
  "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
  "total_duration_s": 76.9333,
  "total_frames_30fps": 2308,
  "segments": [
    {
      "seg_id": "N01",
      "text": "Movies picture gemstone mines as glittering crystal caves. In real underground mines, workers drill through solid grey rock.",
      "rate": "+3%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 0.1,
      "end": 7.77,
      "duration": 7.67,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "Miners listen for the drill bit to suddenly drop into a hollow pocket. Inside, they don't find clean air\u2014they hit sticky wet clay.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 8.01,
      "end": 15.783,
      "duration": 7.773,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "Millions of years ago, superheated mineral fluids cooled inside sealed granite cavities. Thick pocket clay cushioned razor-sharp emeralds, tourmaline, and fluorite as they grew.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 16.043,
      "end": 26.226,
      "duration": 10.184,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N04",
      "text": "Only after miners rinse away that grey mud do raw crystal faces flash with color. Yet above ground, jewelers slice out cloudy specks as worthless flaws.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 26.486,
      "end": 35.885,
      "duration": 9.399,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N05",
      "text": "To deep-Earth geologists, those rejected flaws are priceless. Some rough diamonds blast upward through volcanic pipes from more than six hundred kilometers down.",
      "rate": "+2%",
      "pitch": "+1Hz",
      "start": 36.145,
      "end": 45.432,
      "duration": 9.287,
      "pause_after": 0.26,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N06",
      "text": "Firing X-ray beams into flawed diamonds, scientists found ringwoodite\u2014a deep mineral locking away water. In twenty eighteen, diamonds even revealed Ice-Seven: solid high-pressure water ice.",
      "rate": "+1%",
      "pitch": "+0Hz",
      "start": 45.692,
      "end": 57.615,
      "duration": 11.923,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N07",
      "text": "That doesn't mean an open underground ocean sloshes beneath Earth's crust. Most of that deep water stays trapped inside crystal rock and microscopic fluid pockets.",
      "rate": "-2%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 57.895,
      "end": 67.243,
      "duration": 9.347,
      "pause_after": 0.28,
      "emphasis_words": []
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N08",
      "text": "Jewelers polish away tiny inclusions for sparkle. Scientists read those same crystal traps as time capsules\u2014carried up through solid mine rock.",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
      "start": 67.523,
      "end": 76.703,
      "duration": 9.181,
      "pause_after": 0.24,
      "emphasis_words": []
    }
  ],
